@@ -327,6 +328,11 @@ the chat transcript.
   terminal navigation actions. The right pane keeps the chat prompt visible while scroll offsets
   reveal earlier transcript rows.
 
+In command mode, `TerminalUi` supports vim-style visual selection in the focused pane. `v`, `V`, and
+Ctrl-V start character, line, and block selections; `h/j/k/l` and arrow keys move the visual cursor;
+`y` copies the selected text and `Y` forces linewise copy. Copied text is stored in the terminal UI
+clipboard state and emitted through an OSC 52 terminal clipboard control sequence on the next render.
+
 `src/ui_harness.rs::UiHarness` is the test harness for terminal behavior. It exercises the same
 `TerminalUi` frame path used by the interactive example. UI tests should drive
 `UiHarness::handle_byte` or `UiHarness::handle_bytes` rather than duplicating terminal input logic.
